# Example Rule

This is an example of a user rule. Rules are persistent instructions that
apply on top of your Agent Mode prompt.

## How to Use Rules

1. Copy this file and rename it (remove `.example` extension)
2. Edit the content to add your instructions
3. Rules are loaded in alphabetical order by filename
4. Prefix with numbers for explicit ordering: `01-first.md`, `02-second.md`

## Example Rule Content

Always use type hints in Python function signatures.

Prefer dataclasses over plain classes when appropriate.

When writing tests, use descriptive test names that explain the behavior.
